---
3md: 1.0
axis: skill
agent: fledge-cli-tester
tools: cargo, fledge
persona: builds fledge from source and exercises its real CLI surface via magpie's rune-wrapped driver
---
Dogfoods CorvidLabs/magpie's CLI target against fledge itself: builds
this PR's binary from source, then runs it through `fledge rune run` —
the stable, separately-installed magpie driver — so every invocation is
captured exactly as a real terminal would see it. Two distinct "fledge"s
here on purpose: the driver (stable, installed by magpie's reusable
workflow) wraps the subject (this PR's own freshly-built binary).

Every `tool=` below is a bare command (no `{placeholder}`) on purpose —
magpie's generic --specs-dir engine only executes bare commands. See
CorvidLabs/magpie's README, "Using this in another repo."

@plane z=0 label="fledge-cli-tester" kind=identity
# fledge-cli-tester

Build first; everything else exercises the freshly-built binary, never
the separately-installed driver.

@plane z=1 label="build" kind=skill triggers="build, compile, cargo" tool="cargo build --release --locked" cost="build"
# Skill: build

Compiles this PR's fledge from source. Everything downstream depends on
this having succeeded.

@plane z=2 label="version" kind=skill triggers="version" tool="fledge rune run --timeout=15 --json -- ./target/release/fledge --version" cost="proc"
# Skill: version

Asserts the freshly-built binary reports a version string. Requires
[[z=1|build]].

@plane z=3 label="help" kind=skill triggers="help, usage" tool="fledge rune run --timeout=15 --json -- ./target/release/fledge --help" cost="proc"
# Skill: help

Asserts --help exits cleanly and prints real usage text. Requires
[[z=1|build]].
